n it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 11.0% year on year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025), reaching $313.2m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $277.7m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026030740/0001628280-26-030740-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-030740"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-19.4% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 43.4% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-19.6% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $11.1m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1795250/000162828026051125/0001628280-26-051125-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-051125"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -4.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.04,"consecutive":2,"current":0.11,"current_display":"11.0%","threshold_display":"-4.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.194,"current_display":"-19.4%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.35,"current_display":"0.35","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal to interpret. It is the exit.","editable":false}],"team":[{"raw_name":"James Lawrence Dolan","role":"Officer","title_filed":"Executive Chairman and CEO","shares":null,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bought_in_win